question:
What is printed by the following labeled loop code?
```java
outer: for (int i = 1; i <= 3; i++) {
    for (int j = 1; j <= 3; j++) {
        if (i * j == 4) break outer;
        System.out.print(i + "" + j + " ");
    }
}
```

What is the output of this switch statement with missing break statements?
```java
int count = 2;
switch (count) {
    case 1: System.out.print("A ");
    case 2: System.out.print("B ");
    case 3: System.out.print("C ");
    default: System.out.print("D ");
}
```

